# Recut Project Agent Guide

You are working inside a Recut project through its MCP Host.

## Required turn protocol

1. Call `recut.project_context` before reasoning about project state.
2. Call `tools/list` before selecting an App tool. `recut.project_context` already includes the configured media contract; use the default route unless the user explicitly requests another route.
3. Report Artifact IDs after creation.

## Media reply protocol

When `recut.image.generate` returns completed `assetIds`, when `recut.video.generate_async` accepts a video task and returns its stable `assetIds`, or when `recut.media.get_job` reports a completed speech job, include one XML media reference for every asset in the final user-facing reply. A submitted video Asset may still be `running`; its Recut `assetId` is already valid and will update in place:

`<media type="image|video|audio" assetid="ASSET_ID"/>`

Use `image` for `recut.image.generate`, `video` for `recut.video.generate_async`, and `audio` for `recut.speech.generate_async`. The Recut chat UI renders only these controlled references as previews; never invent an asset ID, never replace the tag with a filesystem path or URL, and keep a short human-readable explanation beside the tag.

The CLI runs non-interactively with approvals bypassed inside the local Recut host. This authorizes tool execution only; it does not authorize guessing, destructive work, or actions outside the current project.

## Video generation boundary

Before choosing a skill or implementation, classify the request from the current App workflow. A workflow stage that asks for a generated image, video, or speech asset is a platform media job. Use the Recut MCP media tools: `recut.image.generate`, `recut.video.generate_async`, `recut.speech.generate_async`, and `recut.media.get_job`.

Keep user-configured extensions available. A platform media job is a provider invocation, not a local video-authoring task: do not select or read a generic video-creation skill for it, even when one is automatically suggested. HyperFrames is relevant only when the user explicitly asks to author or render a HyperFrames composition; it is not the implementation path for an App workflow stage that asks for a generated video asset. Do not substitute a generated Scene with HyperFrames, ffmpeg, browser automation, shell scripts, or local rendering. A Scene relationship is complete as soon as `recut.video.generate_async` is accepted and returns a stable Recut video `assetId`; persist that reference immediately, then use `recut.media.get_job` only to report the Asset's later `running`/`completed`/`failed` state.

## Current App Source

The current App package is mounted at `.recut/app`. It is a shared source checkout, not a copy: inspect its `manifest.json`, `AGENTS.md`, references, UI, and implementation there when they are relevant. You may improve App source when the user requests it; check its Git state first and validate the App after editing. Do not treat App source rollback as permission to delete or roll back project databases, media, or user-created files.

